cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'SOP-SSFCM: spatial opinion-pooling semi-supervised fuzzy c-means (reference implementation)'
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Xuan Hoang
  - family-names: Mai
    given-names: Dinh Sinh
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Long Giang
repository-code: https://github.com/longlinh/SOP-SSFCM_Algs
abstract: >-
  NumPy reference implementation of SOP-SSFCM, a semi-supervised fuzzy c-means
  whose distance is augmented by a fixed spatial prior obtained as the
  logarithmic opinion pool of classifier class probabilities over the pixel
  neighbourhood, together with the unpooled control (r = 0), a self-contained
  synthetic demonstration and the scripts that reproduce the benchmark.
keywords:
  - fuzzy c-means
  - semi-supervised clustering
  - hyperspectral image
  - opinion pooling
  - classifier guidance
  - few labeled samples
license: MIT
version: 2.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-05'
